WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.370
. This is very exciting, but also a little
bit depressing because it's not going to pass

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.490
the Senate.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:13.620
House and Senate Democrats have introduced
legislation to make Washington, DC a state,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.840
the fifty first state of the United States.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.539
This is something we've been talking about
for months and months.

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:25.420
The measure was reintroduced in the House
by a delegate, Eleanor Holmes Norton.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.740
She's a Democrat who represents the District
of Columbia.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:35.750
And the Senate version was introduced by Senator
Tom Carper from Delaware as of Tuesday evening.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:41.690
Norton says she has more than 200 co-sponsors
in the House, but it appears as though there

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:48.080
is no chance whatsoever that this is going
to pass in the Senate.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.960
Democrats control the Senate with the 50/50
split and Kamala Harris as a tie breaking

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.050
vote.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:01:00.000
But Democrats would need to overcome a filibuster
on this issue, which requires 60 votes.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.369
This is not something you can pass via budget
reconciliation, meaning Democrats need to

00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:06.749
find ten Republicans willing to vote yes.

00:01:06.749 --> 00:01:10.170
Washington, D.C. should meet should be a state.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:14.090
Republican lawmakers for a long time have
opposed Washington, D.C. statehood.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:20.740
As you and I have talked about before, representation
in Washington, D.C. would likely be overwhelmingly

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.840
Democratic, meaning two additional Democratic
senators.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.500
And that is not something that Republicans
want to see.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.259
Now, of course, the reality is that on the
merits, this makes obvious sense, even by

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:36.789
Republicans so-called values if the Republican
Party were actually principled.

00:01:36.789 --> 00:01:41.700
This should be a unanimous vote in favor of
Washington, D.C., being a state.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.780
Washington, D.C. is being taxed without representation.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:55.969
Big government is ruling over these Washington,
D.C. folks without them having a voice.

00:01:55.969 --> 00:02:02.700
If this were Utah that didn't have two senators,
Republicans would have voted, I don't know,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.369
decades ago and said, oh, Utah absolutely
must have two senators.

00:02:06.369 --> 00:02:10.679
But the difference is Utah's very red and
Washington, D.C. is very blue.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:16.010
But if the principle here is that people deserve
representation, you're paying taxes.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:21.920
Why do some taxpayers get Senate representation
and other taxpayers do not?

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.430
It is because they know who lives in Washington,
D.C. and they know how Washington, D.C. would

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:27.430
vote.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.210
And so it's not really about principles or
democracy anymore.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.760
If you are an American, you should have at
least one member of the House representing

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.980
you and two senators.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.709
How is this even a debate?

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:46.459
Well, it's a debate because of the false claims
of values and principles when it's convenient

00:02:46.459 --> 00:02:51.959
to them for Republicans and abandoning those
same principles when it no longer is convenient.

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:58.750
Washington, D.C. has more than 100000 more
people living in it than the entire state

00:02:58.750 --> 00:02:59.909
of Wyoming.

00:02:59.909 --> 00:03:05.390
OK, if Washington, D.C. was a state, they
would have their own National Guard.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:12.280
They could have responded on January 6th without
having to depend on all of these other players

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:15.230
to say, fine, fine, fine, we're going to send
National Guard.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:19.970
Washington, D.C. is the 20th largest city
in the United States.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.550
That's not even the D.C. metro.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.799
That's Washington, D.C. itself.

00:03:23.799 --> 00:03:25.690
They pay federal taxes.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.560
They pay local you know, they pay all sorts
of taxes, but they have no senators.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.730
It is absolutely ridiculous.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:36.810
And I hope that Joe Biden will actually make
this an issue.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:43.330
There have been questions about is how much
of a of an issue is this going to be for the

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.409
Biden Harris administration?

00:03:45.409 --> 00:03:49.269
The people of Washington, D.C., deserve to
be represented just as much as the people

00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:50.519
of other states.

00:03:50.519 --> 00:03:52.081
We know why Republicans aren't for it.

00:03:52.081 --> 00:03:57.219
It is not for any principle other than the
principle of we are hypocrites and just do

00:03:57.219 --> 00:03:59.609
things that favor our party.

00:03:59.609 --> 00:04:06.280
That's the only principle that Republicans
are abiding by and adhering to when they say,

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.310
yeah, we don't think Washington, D.C. should
be a state.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:14.189
Now, we've talked also about Puerto Rico,
Puerto Rico, I believe both D.C. and Puerto

00:04:14.189 --> 00:04:15.640
Rico should be states.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:16.870
If Puerto Rico wants to be a state.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:22.789
Of course, the difference is politically and
again, for me, it's the principle.

00:04:22.789 --> 00:04:24.210
So I don't care about this.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:30.300
It's less clear that Puerto Rico would probably
not be unanimously Democratic and has representation.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.220
It's there's a larger conservative contingent
in Puerto Rico.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:39.490
I would expect that there would probably be
at least one member of the House that is a

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:43.419
Republican that would win in Puerto Rico Senate.

00:04:43.419 --> 00:04:44.750
I don't know.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:50.490
But the principle here makes me come to no
other conclusion than D.C. should be a state.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.780
Puerto Rico should be a state.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.210
Now, I know people will say, well, what about
American Samoa?

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.210
What about Guam?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:58.880
OK, we're dealing with Puerto Rico and Washington,
DC right now.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.580
Send me your thoughts about this.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:06.000
What could convince ten, ten Republicans in
the Senate to say, yeah, I will vote for D.C.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.330
statehood?

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.330
Let me know your thoughts.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:13.560
We'll have continued coverage of this on our
Instagram page at The David Pakman Show.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:06:01.870
And you can follow me on Instagram as well
